TASK-190 runtime harness: the sidebar's tab hover card. Temporary code, never
committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task190-harness.patch
    xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    OUT="$PWD/.derived-logs/task190"; mkdir -p "$OUT"
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify190 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # wait for the "done" line in $OUT/verify.log (about 110 s), then kill that pid.
    # "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber> <panelNumber> <x,y,w,h>" lines are for a
    # watcher that runs `screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber>` (and the panel's
    # number, and -R for the region holding both) within about 2 s.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task190-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

Seeds seven tabs (network pages), shows each in turn so leaving it captures
its switcher preview (and the disk thumbnail), then pins one (live pinned
row), pins and closes another (dormant pinned row with a thumbnail on disk),
favourites one and splits two. Hover is driven through the cells' and tiles'
own mouseEntered / mouseMoved / mouseExited (posted mouseMoved events give no
tracking-area enter or exit), in light then dark: a normal row, the selected
row (no thumbnail, immediate swap from the previous row), the live pinned
row, the dormant pinned row, each half of the split and the favourite tile.
Then dismissals: a posted mouse down, a posted key down, a scroll CGEvent
posted to the app's own pid, resign key (makeKey on another window; the
delegate method directly when that cannot make it key) and Cmd+S-style
sidebar hide; then a hover-revealed sidebar (sidebarHoverZoneEntered with
sidebarPointerProbeForTesting) and its auto-hide. Every card is logged with
its text, thumbnail frame, panel frame, the sidebar's visible frame and the
gap between them; a 120 Hz sampler logs when the card shows and hides.

Results (2026-10-24, screen locked for the whole session, so no window
captures and no pixels checked): every row kind showed the expected text and
thumbnail (none for the selected tab), 260 pt wide, 6 pt right of the
sidebar's visible edge, top level with the row; fresh hovers showed after
0.458-0.462 s, row-to-row and split-half moves swapped at once; mouse down,
key down, resign key and sidebar hide each hid the card within ~10 ms and it
stayed hidden on that row; the hover-revealed sidebar showed the card and its
auto-hide took it away. The scroll leg did not reach the monitor: the
CGEvent-built NSEvent had no window and the postToPid event was not delivered
while locked.

Re-run unlocked (2026-10-24, run6): capture each SHOOT with
`screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber>` and `screencapture -x -l <panelNumber>`
(the panel capture comes out composited over the window, which is the useful
picture; -R region captures pick up whatever window is in front, since a
shell-launched app stays behind). Seen: every card kind in light and dark,
6 pt outside the sidebar, top level with the row; the selected row's compact
card; split halves; the favourite tile; the hover-revealed sidebar. The glass
takes its tint from what is behind it (a light card over a white page in dark
mode), like the palette and the Control+Tab switcher, which use the same
GlassContainerView. The scroll leg still did not reach the monitor (the
postToPid scroll is not delivered to a window that is not frontmost).

